  "id": "Compound::DB00774 - Gene::760",
  "verbalization": "Hydroflumethiazide is implicated in the regulation of calcium through a series of binding interactions that ultimately lead to the binding of calcium ions (Ca2). The evidence suggests that Hydroflumethiazide binds to Ca4, which is then bound by Benzthiazide or Cyclothiazide, both of which in turn bind to Ca2. This chain of binding events places Hydroflumethiazide in a functional relationship with Ca2, particularly within the context of thiazide diuretics. The shared lowest common ancestors, such as Thiazide Diuretic and Benzothiadiazine, further reinforce the structural and functional link between Hydroflumethiazide and calcium regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Hydroflumethiazide in modulating calcium levels through a complex network of interactions, suggesting a potential mechanism by which it influences cellular processes involving calcium homeostasis.",
